    "reason": "The assigned POS for the English lemma 'just' as a verb is highly unusual for a core vocabulary concept; 'just' is predominantly used as an adjective (meaning fair/righteous) or an adverb (meaning only/recently/exactly). The assigned POS for the Japanese expression '当然' as a verb is incorrect; '当然' is an adjectival noun (形容動詞) or an adverb, not a verb. Consequently, the semantic alignment between 'just' (verb) and '当然' (verb) is completely wrong. '当然' means 'natural,' 'right,' or 'as a matter of course,' which aligns with the *adjective* sense of 'just,' not the rare verb sense ('to justify' or 'to adjust'). This entry has fundamental errors in both POS assignments and semantic alignment based on those assignments.",
